  "step_2": "The individual states that 'the balance is roughly the same' between A and B and that they chose to take the risk of losing more in A. This indicates that the individual perceived the expected value of both lotteries as similar. The individual did not mention any explicit calculation of probable outcomes or their average. Instead, the focus is on risk-taking — choosing the lottery with higher potential loss (A) despite the same expected value. The justification is based on risk preference, not on the concept of probable outcomes or their average. The individual does not refer to probabilities above 1/n (where n is the number of outcomes) or any evaluation of which outcomes are probable. The deliberation centers on risk aversion or risk-seeking behavior, not on the formal rule of probable outcomes.",
